# s2b-stores -> CORE-WIRE-G2 (lead applies, then deletes this file)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-connections/Cargo.toml

`[dependencies]` (merge with the lines other s2b tasks add; mixdog-ssh, mixdog-core-api, mixdog-protocol and reqwest are there already):

    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-statefile = { workspace = true }
    serde = { workspace = true }
    serde_json = { workspace = true }
    sha2 = { workspace = true }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "sync", "macros"] }
    tracing = { workspace = true }
    url = { workspace = true }
    uuid = { workspace = true, features = ["v4"] }

`[dev-dependencies]` (merge with the section other s2b tasks add):

    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }
    mixdog-testkit = { workspace = true }
    tempfile = { workspace = true }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "sync", "macros", "net", "io-util", "time"] }

(`url` and `uuid` are `[workspace.dependencies]` entries already, both in the lock; `uuid` has `v4` on in mixdog-core-session. `reqwest`
needs no `json` feature: the redeem and presence calls send and read bytes. No new crate in the lock; `cargo hakari generate` after.)

