## Calls into other tasks (names to reconcile, not edited here)

host_store.rs calls `mixdog_ssh::command::parse_ssh_target(&str) -> Result<SshTarget, SshTargetError>` and reads
`SshTarget.display` (String), `SshTarget::key()` and `SshTarget::label()` (as s2b-ssh-base defines them in command.rs).
If that shape changes, only `target_id` in host_store.rs changes.

remote_hosts.rs `fetch_host_presence` answers `HashMap<host id, bool>` (not the `HashSet<id>` the plan wrote): `false` is a
host its relay reports offline, an absent id a relay that could not answer, as the desktop's `Map<string, boolean>` did
(the remote window shows `online: null` for unknown).

host_store.rs keeps its own `SshHostSettings` (the parse/validate of `parseHostSettings` and the file's field order live with the store
that persists them). s2b-ssh-base lists `context::HostSettings`: the connection code should convert from `SshHostSettings` (or
`HostSettings` should become a re-export of it) so there is one definition of the fields.

Stores take the `DurabilityIo` lane token the composition root holds: `SshHostStore::load(&paths, io).await`,
`RemoteHostStore::load(&paths, io).await`, `PortForwardStore::new(&paths, io)`, `WindowRestoreStore::new(&paths, io)`.

## Registration / SERVICE_PENDING

None: this task registers no protocol method and composes no service (s2b-service does).
